-- title:
--   Residue discs of an affine chart: disjoint, cusp-free, equivariant (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), let $s$ be a member of $W$, and assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ via `hle`. Let $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q$, $K_b$ an intermediate field of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $A_b$ the valuation subring of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, assumed a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi_b$. Then, $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ being a $k_0$-algebra in the evident way, for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, every subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure, which contains the image of $j$ (the coefficient embedding of `jq`, transported by `hle`) and is stable under all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\zeta : \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every field $F_{ss}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with residue map onto $F_{ss}$ such that $B \subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$ and every element of $F_{ss}$ is a quotient of residues of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator, every finite set $N$ of places $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ characterised by: $Q \notin N$ iff all residues of elements of $B$ lie in the valuation subring of $Q$, and $N$ stable under the residue automorphisms $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ attached to elements $\tau$ of the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms which preserve $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and all families $S_\bullet$ of subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, $\varphi_\bullet : \mathrm{Polynomial}\,A_b \to S_\bullet$, $\chi_\bullet : S_\bullet \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ satisfying, for each $Q \notin N$, the hypotheses summarised here as: $S_Q$ contains the image of $A_b$ and $\varphi_Q$ sends $C(a)$ to it, $\chi_Q\varphi_Q C =$ the residue of $A$, $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q X) = 0$, $S_Q$ is local with $\ker \chi_Q$ its maximal ideal, $S_Q$ lies in the compositum of $k_0(K_b)$ and $F_0$ and has that compositum as its field of fractions, $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type, the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ meets $S_Q$ in the multiples of $\varphi_Q(C\,\varpi_b)$, $\chi_Q$ computes the residue at $Q$ of the $R$-residue, $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q X$ equals $1$, and $S_Q$ is exactly $\{g/h : g,h \in B,\$ the residue of $h$ has nonzero value at $Q\}$, in particular contains $B$; and, with $D_Q$ the set of places $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that are rational, satisfy $S_Q \subseteq P.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$ for $f \in S_Q$, and for which $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $< 1$ exactly when $\chi_Q f = 0$: the conclusion is that (i) for $Q, Q' \notin N$, if some $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ then $Q = Q'$; (ii) for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of $j$ is $\ge 0$; and (iii) for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms which preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and every $Q$, one has $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot Q \in N$ iff $Q \in N$, and if $Q \notin N$ then $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(D_Q) = \{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_Q\}$ equals $D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot Q}$.
--
--   This is the $q=2$ case of the statement that the residue discs attached to the smooth points of an affine chart of the reduction are pairwise disjoint, contain no cusp (the $j$-function has non-negative order on them) and are permuted by the level automorphisms compatibly with the induced permutation of the ends. It feeds the construction of supersingular discrete valuation rings and of the stalks at base smooth points on the Igusa leg of the semistable covering, and is used by three downstream results of that construction.
